<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ōuchi clan</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Ōuchi were a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samurai">samurai</a> clan of western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a>, based in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/suo-province">Suō Province</a>, who claimed descent from a prince of the Korean kingdom of Baekje. As military governors they built a powerful domain around Yamaguchi, dominated trade with Ming <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/korea">Korea</a>, and patronised learning and the arts. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ouchi-yoshitaka">Ōuchi Yoshitaka</a> was overthrown by his retainer <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sue-harukata">Sue Harukata</a> in 1551, and the Mōri destroyed the last of the line in 1557.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ouchi-clan.jpg" alt="Ōuchi clan" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Mukai · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Japanese_Crest_Oouchi_Hisi.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
